# The Weekly Challenge 292 - Lubos Kolouch

Solutions for Task 1 (Twice Largest) and Task 2 (Zuma Game) in Perl and Python.

## Task 1: Twice Largest
- Determine if the unique largest integer in an array is at least twice as large as every other element.
- Return its index, or -1 otherwise.
- Implemented in $O(N)$ linear time and $O(1)$ extra space in Perl and Python.

## Task 2: Zuma Game
- Find the minimum number of insertions from hand required to eliminate all balls on the board.
- Implemented using Breadth-First Search (BFS) with state hashing and regex-based group elimination.
